{"entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "primaryAccession": "Q9NS82", "secondaryAccessions": ["B2RE84"], "uniProtkbId": "AAA1_HUMAN", "entryAudit": {"firstPublicDate": "2002-11-15", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2026-06-10", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "2000-10-01", "entryVersion": 177, "sequenceVersion": 1}, "annotationScore": 5.0, "organism": {"scientificName": "Homo sapiens", "commonName": "Human", "taxonId": 9606, "lineage": ["Eukaryota", "Metazoa", "Chordata", "Craniata", "Vertebrata", "Euteleostomi", "Mammalia", "Eutheria", "Euarchontoglires", "Primates", "Haplorrhini", "Catarrhini", "Hominidae", "Homo"]}, "proteinExistence": "1: Evidence at protein level", "proteinDescription": {"recommendedName": {"fullName": {"value": "Asc-type amino acid transporter 1"}, "shortNames": [{"value": "Asc-1"}]}, "alternativeNames": [{"fullName": {"value": "Solute carrier family 7 member 10"}}]}, "genes": [{"geneName": {"value": "SLC7A10"}, "synonyms": [{"value": "ASC1"}]}], "comments": [{"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P63115"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P63116"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "10863037"}], "value": "Associates with SLC3A2/4F2hc to form a functional heterodimeric complex that translocates small neutral L- and D-amino acids across the plasma membrane. Preferentially mediates exchange transport, but can also operate via facilitated diffusion (By similarity) (PubMed:10863037). Acts as a major transporter for glycine, L- and D-serine in the central nervous system. At the spinal cord and brainstem regulates glycine metabolism and glycinergic inhibitory neurotransmission by providing for glycine de novo synthesis from L-serine and glycine recycling from astrocytes to glycinergic motor neurons (By similarity). At Schaffer collateral-CA1 synapses mediates D-serine and glycine release that modulates post-synaptic activation of NMDA receptors and excitatory glutamatergic transmission (By similarity). May regulate D-serine release from mesenchymal progenitors located in developing subcutaneous adipose tissue, favoring white adipocyte over thermogenic beige adipocyte lineage commitment (By similarity)"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION"}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "L-alanine(in) + glycine(out) = L-alanine(out) + glycine(in)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:74019"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:57305"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:57972"}], "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P63115"}]}}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "L-serine(out) + L-alanine(in) = L-serine(in) + L-alanine(out)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:74023"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:33384"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:57972"}], "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P63115"}]}}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "L-threonine(out) + L-alanine(in) = L-threonine(in) + L-alanine(out)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:74027"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:57926"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:57972"}], "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P63115"}]}}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "L-cysteine(out) + L-alanine(in) = L-cysteine(in) + L-alanine(out)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:74031"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:35235"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:57972"}], "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P63115"}]}}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "2-aminoisobutanoate(out) + L-alanine(in) = 2-aminoisobutanoate(in) + L-alanine(out)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:74063"},